kcov-bash53-ansi-c.patch -- teaches kcov v43's bash engine the ANSI-C
quoting bash 5.3 uses in xtrace (base#1030). Applied in the kcov-builder
stage of dockerfile/Dockerfile.test-tools AFTER kcov-76bf685.patch, on
top of which it was generated. Only the diff below is applied (`git
apply` skips this header); if a KCOV_VERSION bump moves its context, the
apply fails and so does the build.

bash 5.3 writes a traced value holding a newline as one line,
`$'line one\n  - \'quoted\' word'`. v43's getInputType flips its
single-quote state on every `'` and honours `\` only outside a quote, so
each `\'` inside `$'...'` flips the state; the line ends "inside a quote"
and every later trace line, coverage marker included, is dropped. The
diff gives `$'` its own state in which a backslash consumes the next
character and only an unescaped `'` closes the string. A plain `'...'`
keeps the literal-backslash rule, so the bash 5.2 form reads as before.

diff --git a/src/engines/bash-engine.cc b/src/engines/bash-engine.cc
index 0d32dbb..20b055b 100644
--- a/src/engines/bash-engine.cc
+++ b/src/engines/bash-engine.cc
@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@ enum InputType
 	INPUT_QUOTE,        // "
 	INPUT_SINGLE_QUOTE, // '
 	INPUT_MULTILINE,    // backslash backslash
+	INPUT_ANSI_C_QUOTE, // $' (bash 5.3 xtrace)
 };
 
 class BashEngine : public ScriptEngineBase
@@ -544,8 +545,21 @@ private:
 		enum InputType out = m_inputType;
 
 		for(std::string::size_type i = 0; i < str.size(); ++i) {
-			if (str[i] == '\\' && out == INPUT_NORMAL)
+			if (out == INPUT_ANSI_C_QUOTE) {
+				// $'...': a backslash escapes the next character, so \' and \\
+				// are consumed whole; only an unescaped ' closes the string.
+				if (str[i] == '\\')
+					i++;
+				else if (str[i] == '\'')
+					out = INPUT_NORMAL;
+			}
+			else if (str[i] == '\\' && out == INPUT_NORMAL)
+				i++;
+			else if (str[i] == '$' && out == INPUT_NORMAL &&
+					i + 1 < str.size() && str[i + 1] == '\'') {
+				out = INPUT_ANSI_C_QUOTE;
 				i++;
+			}
 			else if (str[i] == '\'')
 				out = (out == INPUT_NORMAL ? INPUT_SINGLE_QUOTE : INPUT_NORMAL);
 		}
